<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasmonean dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hasmonean</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hasmonean dynasty ruled Judea in the second and first centuries BCE. It arose from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maccabean-revolt">Maccabean revolt</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>, sparked by religious persecution and Hellenising pressures. Its establishment of an independent Jewish state illustrates the Seleucid Empire's loss of control over its subject peoples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasmonean-dynasty.jpg" alt="Hasmonean dynasty" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antigone II (Mattathiah; roi hasmonéen). Autorité émettrice de monnaie Hasmonéens (dynastie). Autorité émettrice de monnaie … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Monnaie_-_Prutah,_bronze,_J%C3%A9rusalem,_Jud%C3%A9e,_Mattathias_Antigonos_-_btv1b8480202s_(1_of_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
